# The number is line 1; s6 stops reading there, so nothing may precede it.
#
# The service that wedged: an avahi-daemon that never answered its down signal
# held the shutdown open past the Supervisor's 10s and took a SIGKILL with the
# whole container. Nothing bounded that, because s6-supervise waits forever by
# default and the shutdown's `s6-rc -bda change` sets no timeout of its own.
#
# 2000ms is twenty times the slowest of these three services' stops -- avahi's
# own, at under 100ms including its goodbye packets -- so a slow host loses
# nothing to it. The Dockerfile's S6_KILL_GRACETIME comment carries the
# arithmetic for the whole shutdown against the 10s.
